# Byte-compiled / editor cruft
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# Cached per-subject trial arrays written by `hpc_block_cv.py prepare`, and
# per-subject output directories written by the `task` stage. The cache is
# ~25 KB per subject and rebuilds from the database in minutes, so there is no
# reason to version it. Note it is also the one artefact in this project that
# is NOT reproducible across time: running the identical COHORT_QUERY months
# apart has returned a disjoint set of animals, because the upstream database
# contents changed. Treat a cache as belonging to one analysis run.
cache*/
out*/

# Written automatically by the resume guards, never by hand:
#   *_old_*      a results CSV whose schema predates the current RESULT_COLUMNS
#   *_partial_*  a subject that was scored only partially, moved aside because
#                its shared volatility is the median over ALL its placements
*_old_*.csv
*_partial_*.csv

# Scratch figures written to the working directory by the comparison scripts.
# Only the repo root is matched, so curated figures under data/ stay tracked.
/*.png
